{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 📊 Data Collection & Integration\n",
    "\n",
    "## IEEE Project: Phishing Guard v2.0\n",
    "\n",
    "**Objective:** Combine multiple phishing datasets to create a comprehensive training dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Sources:\n",
    "1. **Combined Dataset** - Existing labeled dataset\n",
    "2. **OpenPhish** - Real-time phishing feed\n",
    "3. **PhishTank** - Community-driven phishing database\n",
    "\n",
    "**Author:** [Your Name]  \n",
    "**Date:** February 2025  \n",
    "**Institution:** [Your University]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔧 Step 1: Import Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "We use pandas for data manipulation and yaml for configuration management."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import yaml\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Libraries imported successfully\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## ⚙️ Step 2: Load Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Load project configuration from YAML file. This ensures reproducibility across different environments."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load configuration\n",
    "with open(\"../07_configs/config.yaml\", \"r\") as f:\n",
    "    config = yaml.safe_load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📋 Configuration loaded:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  - Project: {config.get('project_name', 'N/A')}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  - Version: {config.get('version', 'N/A')}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📥 Step 3: Load Individual Datasets\n",
    "\n",
    "Load three different phishing datasets with varying formats:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load datasets\n",
    "df_combined = pd.read_csv(\"01_data/raw/combined_dataset.csv\")\n",
    "df_openphish = pd.read_csv(\"01_data/raw/openphish.txt\", header=None, names=[\"url\"])\n",
    "df_phishtank = pd.read_csv(\"01_data/raw/phishtank.csv\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"📊 Dataset Summary:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  1. Combined Dataset: {len(df_combined):,} samples\")\n",
    "print(f\"  2. OpenPhish Feed: {len(df_openphish):,} samples\")\n",
    "print(f\"  3. PhishTank: {len(df_phishtank):,} samples\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📈 Total URLs: {len(df_combined) + len(df_openphish) + len(df_phishtank):,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔍 Step 4: Explore Dataset Structure\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine the structure of each dataset before integration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Explore combined dataset\n",
    "print(\"Combined Dataset Schema:\")\n",
    "print(df_combined.dtypes)\n",
    "print(\"\\nFirst 5 samples:\")\n",
    "df_combined.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🏷️ Step 5: Standardize Labels\n",
    "\n",
    "Different datasets use different labeling schemes. We standardize all to binary (0 = Legitimate, 1 = Phishing).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Challenge:** Combined dataset has mixed label formats (strings and integers)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check current label formats\n",
    "print(\"Label Analysis:\")\n",
    "print(f\"Combined dataset dtype: {df_combined['label'].dtype}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unique values: {df_combined['label'].unique()[:10]}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Show label distribution\n",
    "if df_combined['label'].dtype == 'object':\n",
    "    print(\"\\nLabel distribution (string):\")\n",
    "    print(df_combined['label'].value_counts())\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nLabel distribution (numeric):\")\n",
    "    print(df_combined['label'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Standardize combined dataset labels\n",
    "if df_combined['label'].dtype == 'object':\n",
    "    df_combined['label'] = df_combined['label'].map({\n",
    "        'phishing': 1, \n",
    "        'legitimate': 0, \n",
    "        '0': 0, \n",
    "        '1': 1\n",
    "    }).fillna(0).astype(int)\n",
    "    print(\"✅ Converted string labels to binary\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df_combined['label'] = df_combined['label'].astype(int)\n",
    "    print(\"✅ Labels already numeric\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFinal label distribution:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Phishing (1): {sum(df_combined['label'] == 1):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Legitimate (0): {sum(df_combined['label'] == 0):,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📊 Step 6: Process OpenPhish Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "OpenPhish contains only phishing URLs, so we assign label = 1 to all samples."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# OpenPhish: all phishing\n",
    "df_openphish[\"label\"] = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"OpenPhish Dataset:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total samples: {len(df_openphish):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  All labeled as phishing (1)\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nSample URLs:\")\n",
    "print(df_openphish['url'].head(3).to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🏦 Step 7: Process PhishTank Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "PhishTank has a 'verified' column we need to map to binary labels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Explore PhishTank structure\n",
    "print(\"PhishTank Columns:\")\n",
    "print(df_phishtank.columns.tolist())\n",
    "print(\"\\nVerified column values:\")\n",
    "print(df_phishtank['verified'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# PhishTank: map 'verified' to 0/1\n",
    "df_phishtank = df_phishtank[[\"url\", \"verified\"]].copy()\n",
    "df_phishtank[\"label\"] = df_phishtank[\"verified\"].map({\"yes\": 1, \"no\": 0}).fillna(0).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"PhishTank after processing:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total samples: {len(df_phishtank):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Phishing: {sum(df_phishtank['label'] == 1):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Legitimate: {sum(df_phishtank['label'] == 0):,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔗 Step 8: Combine All Datasets\n",
    "\n    "Now we merge all three datasets into a unified training dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Combine all datasets\n",
    "df_all = pd.concat([\n",
    "    df_combined[[\"url\", \"label\"]],  # 0/1\n",
    "    df_openphish[[\"url\", \"label\"]],  # 1\n",
    "    df_phishtank[[\"url\", \"label\"]]   # 0/1\n",
    "], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Combined Dataset:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total samples: {len(df_all):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Phishing: {sum(df_all['label'] == 1):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Legitimate: {sum(df_all['label'] == 0):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Class imbalance ratio: {sum(df_all['label'] == 1) / sum(df_all['label'] == 0):.2f}:1\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🧹 Step 9: Remove Duplicates\n",
    "\n    "Remove duplicate URLs that may appear in multiple datasets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Check for duplicates before removal\n",
    "duplicates = df_all.duplicated(subset=[\"url\"]).sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Duplicate URLs found: {duplicates:,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove duplicates\n",
    "df_all = df_all.drop_duplicates(subset=[\"url\"])\n",
    "print(f\"\\nAfter deduplication:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total samples: {len(df_all):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Removed: {duplicates:,} duplicates\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 💾 Step 10: Save Unified Dataset\n",
    "\n    "Save the final dataset to CSV for use in model training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Save to raw directory\n",
    "output_path = \"01_data/raw/combined_dataset.csv\"\n",
    "df_all.to_csv(output_path, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Unified dataset saved successfully!\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n📊 Final Statistics:\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Total samples: {len(df_all):,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Phishing: {sum(df_all['label'] == 1):,} ({sum(df_all['label'] == 1)/len(df_all)*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Legitimate: {sum(df_all['label'] == 0):,} ({sum(df_all['label'] == 0)/len(df_all)*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\n💾 Saved to: {output_path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📈 Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Achievements:**\n",
    "- ✅ Integrated 3 different phishing datasets\n",
    "- ✅ Standardized labels across all sources\n",
    "- ✅ Removed {duplicates:,} duplicate URLs\n",
    "- ✅ Created unified dataset with {len(df_all):,} samples\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next Steps:**\n",
    "1. Data preprocessing (feature extraction)\n",
    "2. Train/validation/test split\n",
    "3. Model training\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data Quality Notes:**\n",
    "- Class imbalance: More phishing than legitimate samples\n",
    "- May need to collect more legitimate URLs for better balance\n",
    "- All URLs are raw text, need feature engineering next"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Display sample of final dataset\n",
    "print(\"\\nSample of Unified Dataset:\")\n",
    "df_all.sample(10, random_state=42)"
   ]
  }
 ],
